<title>NIGERIA: Nigeria to sell electric power to Benin, Togo.</title>
<headline>Nigeria to sell electric power to Benin, Togo.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria's state-run generating company on Monday said it had agreed to sell electric power to tiny West African neighbours Togo and Benin.</p>
<p>A statement from the National Electric Power Authority said it would supply an annual 300 gigawatt hours, subject to a maximum peak demand of 75 megawatts, in line with an agreement signed at the weekend.</p>
<p>The power will be supplied through a 330 kilovolt transmission line between Ikeja in Nigeria and Sakete in Benin.</p>
<p>Nigeria already supplies electric power to its northern neighbour Niger.</p>
<p>-- Lagos newsroom +234 1 2630317</p>
</text>
